    "type_designations": ["CT100 Series", "CT100-B", "CT100-P", "CT100-R", "CT100 PLUS-B", "CT100 PLUS-P"],
    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "Class III, mains-operated, self-indicating, price-computing, single or dual-interval, non-automatic weighing instrument designed for direct sales to the public. Construction: plastic housing, operator's keypad, stainless steel load receptor, operator LCD display, pole-mounted customer LCD display, level indicator, integrated printer (base-mounted on CT100-B and CT100-P; pole-mounted on CT100-R). Devices: initial zero setting device, semi-automatic zero setting device, zero tracking device (around Gross or Net zero), zero indicator, net indicator, stable weight indicator, semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing device, gravity compensation, price-computing, totalisation (including non-weighed items), PLU, fixed weight labelling, multi-vendor operation, calibration/set-up mode via sealed internal switch. Interfaces (some optional): RS232C, cash drawer, USB Device, USB Host, RS485, ZigBee, wired LAN, wireless LAN. Software identified by version number displayed at power-up, shall be 1.xx (xx = non-legally relevant modifications); download not possible without breaking the seal. Load cell, EPROM and calibration switch protected by sealing the enclosure via wire-and-seal or tamper-evident label. Optional Preset Tare device: semi-automatic tare then acts as balancing tare device, with Tare and Preset Tare values limited to Max1. CT100 PLUS variants fitted with a modified integrated printer."
